  "term": "Interpersonal Psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Interpersonal psychotherapy is a form of psychodynamic therapy that focuses on current difficulties in a person’s relationships. It uses ideas from attachment theory to understand how earlier relationships may shape present ones and to help resolve interpersonal problems.",
